# fixedbugs, defect 360, lane cli12, 2026-10-05.
#
# Beside `fixedbugs-360-a-header-that-does-not-compile`: the header compiles
# under clang's own defaults and is refused under the warnings this compiler
# makes errors in every unit, which no group can turn off. Told as the
# header's, and the note says the warning is one the build's flags make an
# error.
#
# **Corrected 2026-10-10, defect 569 (panel 205's R2)**: *which no group can
# turn off* was a policy and is reversed: a header's own code is passed over
# for `-Wall`'s warnings and sign conversions, wherever the header was found,
# and judged for the rest. This header's value narrowed to `int` is one of the
# rest, so it is still refused, and the note says what a header's code is held
# to.

extern "fixedbugs-360-flags.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function thrice(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(thrice(x: 14))
